  "Breadboard hole coordinates were estimated from the circuit image. Rail hole numbers use the nearest column number.",
  "The sensors in the image are two-lead force-sensing resistors, but the parts list maps them to potentiometer-10k. Each uses SIG and VCC, and its GND lead is left unconnected.",
  "The manual lists 10 hook-up wires, but the image shows only 9 jumper wires, so 9 are modelled.",
  "The pushbutton straddles the centre gap. I took side 1 as the left column (col 5) and side 2 as the right column (col 7). Side 1 is wired to 5V and side 2 to pin 2 and the pull-down resistor.",
  "The sensor wired to A0 is pot1 and the one wired to A1 is pot2. They go to breadboard columns 16 and 6, which is how the image routes the yellow wires.",
  "The black Arduino GND wire goes to the second GND header pin (GND.2).",
  "Rail wires link the top and bottom power rails: GND at column 29 and 5V at column 30."
